Line endings: your .editorconfig says end_of_line = crlf, but 795 of 849 C# files are LF as committed and git doesn't convert them: nothing enforced it, so end_of_line = lf is written for C# files and 'format' converts the other 54 (CRLF) to LF where it formats them. To keep CRLF: put 'end_of_line = crlf' below the stylebro-migrate block, in a [*.cs] section (a later line wins; the block's own lines come back on the next init) and run 'bro format' (it rewrites the files), or add '*.cs text eol=crlf' to .gitattributes and run 'git add --renormalize .'.
Final line breaks: your .editorconfig says insert_final_newline = true, and 4 of 849 C# files end without a line break: 'format' adds a last line break to them. To keep that out of the formatting changes, change them in a commit of their own first.
This repository has multi-targeted projects. Run 'bro format' instead of 'dotnet format' here: with IDE0055 on, 'dotnet format' crashes on multi-targeted projects (Roslyn can't merge the target frameworks' copies of a file). The command runs it once per target framework.
